WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.569
SPEAKER: All through
 the evolution of mankind,

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.373
 there has been
 this constant connection.

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:10.142
Woo!

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.313
CHILD: You can see why
this tree's almost dead.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.616
DIRK BRINKMAN: A lot of things
 have happened to it.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.385
♪ (CONTEMPLATIVE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:22.522
SPEAKER 2: When I look out
 at the trees in my backyard,

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.258
 I think about time.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.894
This tree has been alive

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.929
 -longer than Nona and--
-CHILD: Me?

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.530
SPEAKER 2:
 Oh, definitely than you.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.700
This is a vine.
It's gobbling everything up.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.103
It's just like there's a war.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:41.040
GEORGE WEYERHAEUSER: Timber,

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.177
 it's always been a big thing
 in my life,

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.780
 back to my great grandfather.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.151
 I don't know whether it didn't
 lead to my kidnapping, too.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.388
BETH MOON: The first trees
 I photographed,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.692
 I was just drawn to
 how fragile they are.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.133
SPEAKER 3: It's called
 an internment camp,

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.935
 but it was really
 a concentration camp.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.705
SPEAKER 4: "If I can
 bring life to this tree

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.874
 and have hope,

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.310
 maybe one day we'll get out."

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.347
SPEAKER 5:
 My father bought my mother
 this cherry blossom tree.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.651
 All of the freedom that
 he didn't have in the world,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.586
 he poured into that land.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.823
SPEAKER: Cold, heat, fire,
 volcano.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.560
The tree could die,
or the tree could live.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.394
Be gentle.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:37.296
SPEAKER: But it's always going
 to carry the scar of it.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:38.598
CHILD: It's coming! It's coming!

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:42.702
SPEAKER: It just builds
 on itself with time

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.004
 to become this.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.639
That's a story.

